p = "experiments/E320_soft-attach-replaces-snap/experiment.md"
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
def rep(old, new):
    global s
    assert s.count(old) == 1, (old[:60], s.count(old))
    s = s.replace(old, new)

rep('''## 0. The card (what the tools run)''', '''**Amended before the run, 2026-11-12 night, after the critic pass** (ar-critic on d4ee35e6 / 7386e0e1: no blocker; the run E320.a_s<S> has not started, the numbers of the rule are unchanged unless noted). Reasons, in the order of the critic's items: (S3) the arm carries the geometry loss and the controls do not, so the verdict is about the recipe, not about the attachment alone (section 1, "Attribution"); (S4) "the curve touches a delivered piece end by construction" and "pair recall / precision unchanged by construction" were wrong and are corrected (section 1; the docstring of `Attach` and the README row of `jends.py` too); (S5, S7) three more report items (long links dropped, curves, wired ends; the attached-end error on the VAL dump); (S6) the CUT clause, the junction guard and a `better` map for the lower-is-better guards are made explicit; (S8) the kill criterion of the log is read afterwards, not enforced; code (S1) a `--attach` score without `--thr` can no longer overwrite the card of record `ends_card.json`, (S2) `--geom-w > 0` without the polylines in the batch is an error instead of a silent skip.

## 0. The card (what the tools run)''')
rep(''' "prediction": {"value": -0.005, "vs": "c"},
 "arms": {
  "c": {"recipe": "control = E312 of the same seed, read out with the snap''', ''' "prediction": {"value": -0.005, "vs": "c"},
 "better": {"dup_frac": "lower", "vert100_dp": "lower"},
 "arms": {
  "c": {"recipe": "control = E312 of the same seed, read out with the snap''')
rep('''"kill": "the loss is not finite, the attachment cross entropy (`att_ce` of the training log) is not below 1.0 at step 1000 (the candidates are not separable), or the maps after the joint training are worse than E307 by more than 0.05 keypoint F1 on either seed",''', '''"kill": "the loss is not finite, the attachment cross entropy (`att_ce` of the training log) is not below 1.0 at step 1000 (the candidates are not separable), or the maps after the joint training are worse than E307 by more than 0.05 keypoint F1 on either seed (read afterwards, see the by-hand paragraph: the run is not stopped early)",''')
# by hand paragraph
rep('''**KEEP (the snap is replaced at no loss)** when, on BOTH seeds, topo F1 of arm a is at least E312 snapped minus 0.01 (that is above +0.0466 / +0.0515 over the plain graph) AND above the unsnapped E312 plus 0.02 (above +0.0379 / +0.0433), with the guards held (F1@1.0, dup_frac, vertices, junction F1 against c). TIE kept when a is above u + 0.02 but below c - 0.01 on one seed or both (the attachment helps but does not replace the snap: the rule step stays, the next card refines the candidates); CUT when a is not above u + 0.02 or a guard breaks.''', '''**KEEP (the snap is replaced at no loss)** when, on BOTH seeds, topo F1 of arm a is at least E312 snapped minus 0.01 (that is above +0.0466 / +0.0515 over the plain graph) AND above the unsnapped E312 plus 0.02 (above +0.0379 / +0.0433), with the guards held (F1@1.0, dup_frac, vertices, junction F1 against c). TIE kept when a is above u + 0.02 but below c - 0.01 on one seed or both (the attachment helps but does not replace the snap: the rule step stays, the next card refines the candidates); CUT when a is not above u + 0.02 **on either seed** or a guard breaks. Notes on the rule (amendment): (1) the clause "above u + 0.02" is redundant for KEEP (a above c - 0.01 and c above u by 0.0387 / 0.0383 already imply it) and only separates TIE from CUT. (2) **The junction guard is meant to bind:** max_loss 0.03 against E312 snapped (junction F1 0.3194 / 0.3143) means a needs at least 0.2894 / 0.2843 while the unsnapped wiring gives 0.2511 / 0.2474; if topo F1 passes and this guard fails the verdict is CUT by the written rule (not KEEP, not TIE) and the numbers are reported: the snap gains +0.07 junction F1 and an attachment that matches the topo F1 without it has not replaced the snap. (3) The prediction (-0.005 against c) sits 0.005 from the KEEP bound (-0.01): close to a coin flip near the bound, by the numbers alone. (4) `better` map: dup_frac and vert100_dp are lower-is-better, so `max_loss` there means "not more than 0.01 / 1.0 higher"; the verdict is by hand, this map makes `decide.py` read the guards right if it is ever run on these cards.''')
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(s)
print("part 1 ok")
